      {
        "number": 9,
        "internalPageId": 9,
        "title": "It is common to use verbs that state preferences when we talk about hobbies. Check the following chart.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "It is common to use verbs that state preferences when we talk about hobbies. Check the following chart.",
          "MOST COMMON VERBS FOR PREFERENCES NEGATIVE COUNTERPARTS EXAMPLES LIKE DISLIKE / DON’T LIKE She likes eating ice cream. ENJOY DON’T ENJOY I don’t enjoy cooking. LOVE HATE I love listening to music.",
          "TO BE FOR PREFERENCES NEGATIVE COUNTERPARTS EXAMPLES TO BE FOND OF NOT TO BE FOND OF I am fond of playing soccer. TO BE A FAN OF NOT TO BE A FAN OF I am not a fan of watching horror movies. TO BE THRILLED ABOUT NOT TO BE THRILLED ABOUT I am thrilled about reading books.",
          "HINT Notice that after a preference expression, the action can go in ing form."
        ],
        "links": [],
        "media": [
          {
