      {
        "number": 11,
        "internalPageId": 11,
        "title": "Language Targets",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Language Targets",
          "LIKENESS DEGREES EXAMPLES HIGH LEVEL I love drawing cartoons. She is thrilled about learning languages. MEDIUM LEVEL He enjoys working with numbers. They are fans of running marathons. LOW LEVEL We like dancing every weekend. It is fond of hiding bones in the backyard.",
          "We mainly use simple present to express likes and preferences, but there is an interesting fact we need to consider: likeness degrees.",
          "HINT 1. We can also use like and preference expressions to talk about people, food, etc. (Not only for hobbies) 2. The expression thrilled about sometimes is substituted by crazy about."
        ],
